I liked the gameplay, mostly. This game is okay to spend some time, like an average puzzle game.
But I'm posting a negative review because of these points:
1) no steam cloud support: it's a light game resourcewise, but you can't comfortably move your saves from one pc to another or to a laptop;
2) when you delete this game, the savefiles stored in the unity3d folder stay there as they should, but the game doesn't recognize them if you reinstall it, your saves are just gone for it (maybe there is a workaround to force the game to read them, but a simple puzzle is not worth any such effort);
3) devs completely ignore steam forums.
